INTERPRETATION

This is the first qualified direct transfer of the accepted bounded learned-U
authority from Task-1 into a distinct compositional two-stage Task-2
environment after independently validating that environment with the exact
parent.

The neural model remained blind to:

task identity;
program identity;
stage identity;
phase;
absolute position;
global queue;
evaluator correctness;
future information.

It controlled only 25 percent of the U recruitment probability.

Despite causing 51 realized recruitment transition differences across the
baseline-feasible worlds, it preserved every preregistered pairwise
functional, backlog, stream, cost, recovery, lesion, correctness, repair,
and matching gate.

Therefore the evidence supports:

bounded learned local recruitment behavior is not merely Task-1-specific.

It can causally participate in a different compositional service environment
without retraining and without expanding authority beyond U.

BOUNDARY

Do not increase learned authority automatically.

C/S stay-defect remains exact V0.2.

H remains teacher.

No online learning or recursive self-modification is authorized.

NEXT SCIENTIFIC QUESTION

Per preregistration, increase task distance or perturbation difficulty while
holding learned authority fixed at U_A25.

Choose the smallest discriminating experiment that asks whether the
transferred learned recruitment remains functionally contained when the
organism experiences a stronger local developmental perturbation.

Do not change Task-2 load and perturbation severity simultaneously.

Do not change alpha, weights, OBS-V1, or committed-cell authority.

PLAIN-SPEAK INTERPRETATION

This one worked.

We first proved the two-step task was fair for the hand-written organism.

Then we put the same 25-percent neural recruiter back in on ten completely
new worlds.

The neural recruiter really changed cell-development decisions, but the
organism still kept up with the hand-written parent on every required
measure in every fair comparison.

It did not make wrong answers.

It did not make work expire.

It did not slow recovery.

It did not break repair.

And the network still could not see what task, program, stage, or phase it
was working on.

That is substantially stronger evidence that the learned local recruitment
rule is transferring as a developmental behavior rather than memorizing one
specific task setup.

